WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you stay up
late last night?

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.937
Did you watch election returns?
-I did. I did. I did.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How do you feel?
-I feel...

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.208 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:00:08.208 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you --
I mean, maybe I would say

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:15.148 size:84% position:42%
I would like to use you
as a sort of yardstick,

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.217 line:92%
a sort of -- my gold standard

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
for how I should feel,
emotionally,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.255 line:92%
like, my level of rationality,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:27.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
post-midterm,
post-cable exposure.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You know, projection.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was a hard -- I forgot how
stressful projections are.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.870
-Oh, God, I just wish they would
stop that part, in a way.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I wish it was more --
at the very --

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
They wouldn't say anything
about results,

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:42.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
and at the end of the night,
they would just go,

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:45.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This happened," and you would
just go, "Okay, great."

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And let it just be, like,
on a slow scroll

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:51.451 size:81% position:41%
or just let it sort of
rise to the surface.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, maybe it sort of
appears and then it dissolves.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I feel as if --
And I feel as if

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
two things were happening
last night.

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like one place was
trying to be extremely calm...

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:06.766 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.501 size:75% position:38%
-...if you know what
I'm talking about.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-One outlet.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:13.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then I feel like another
outlet was really lively,

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:18.745
and it felt like maybe, like,
the common space in a dorm.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:20.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Everybody just
kind of -- Yeah.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know -- But I don't know.
How do you feel?

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:25.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The only thing I found very
stressful last night

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
is how every time
something happened,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
they'd go,
"We have a big result."

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:33.159
And you realize they never say,
"This next one is meaningless."

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.595 line:92%
-"We have a meaningless result

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
from a state
that doesn't matter."

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:41.201
Yeah, but, you know, I don't
quite know how to feel either.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I certainly know
I could feel worse.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right, right.
I've said that to myself.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I didn't feel that
two years ago.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. No, no.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.410 line:92%
Two years ago, I didn't say,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, it could
have been worse."

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.379 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. No. Exactly.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, in fact,
it proved to be worse.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:57.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
But on the night,
I couldn't imagine.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:02.555 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You thought, well, yes,
there is some comfort

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in knowing --

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.992
-With that, yeah, so --
But I'm also trepidatious about

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:08.194 size:88% position:44%
what it means -- I mean,
I don't -- based on even

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.530 size:75% position:38%
the events of today,
I don't feel like,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:14.134
"Well, we had a midterm, and
then everything settled down."

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:14.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, this is a question
that I did.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:19.873
I asked so many -- Mostly, I
asked the television last night,

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:22.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
but some people
around me did say,

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.810 line:92%
"That's a good question."

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
When people were --
I wouldn't say gloating,

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:28.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there was, you know,
some people

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:32.986 size:78% position:39%
felt really positive
about this blue wave.

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.087 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Let's call it a wave.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.422 line:92%
And they were saying, you know,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is an opportunity
for the Democrats,

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:39.559 line:92%
you know, to do, A, B, C.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:41.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I kept screaming,
"But what in the next --"

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:42.762 size:88% position:44% line:92%
There's two more months.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, what if he,
for instance,

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:48.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
should fire or ask
the Attorney General

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:50.537 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to, you know --

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"You should resign."
Yeah.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we'd be
better off apart."

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
What about
the remaining two months?

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.646 size:75% position:38% line:92%
It's an opportunity.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a recipe for
all sorts of -- you know?

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And nobody -- Well,
no one on the television

00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
would answer me,
because they couldn't hear me.

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.756 line:92%
-Yeah. And that's really one of

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
the downsides
of television, right?

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.459 size:84% position:42%
Yeah. I mean, everybody
says we're living in

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
the golden age of television,
and you're like,

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.430 size:84% position:42%
"Well, then how come
they won't talk to me?"

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.498 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I know.

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:20.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had --
A long time ago, somebody --

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.634 line:92%
I was telling a story about --

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:25.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, my friend --
he told me this really,

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.873 line:92%
you know, amusing story."

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went ahead
and I told the story.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.144
And then they asked, "You know,
which friend was that?"

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:34.547
And I was like, "I think it was
Johnny Carson told --

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:38.051
Johnny Carson told all of
America this story last night."

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:40.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was my friend.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.290
Yeah, that's totally normal,
and you shouldn't feel weird.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mentioned the
golden age of television.

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:47.460
I want to tell you this, because
everybody says, right now,

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's so many good shows,
and it's so hard to figure out

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:50.630 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
what to watch.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:53.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife and I are watching
"Sex and the City."

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're watching
two episodes a night.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have never watched it.
-Wow!

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.973 line:92%
-Wow! two episodes a night.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was a request
my wife made and said,

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:04.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, this is a show
I've watched a hundred times,

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I feel like you would
understand me better

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.347 line:92%
if you watched this show."

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:10.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to say,
I'm enjoying it so much,

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:14.454
and it is a show that I
underestimated, having not seen,

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
just based on --
-Did somebody say, "Wow"?

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-But I didn't --

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:22.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I will admit,
and, obviously, I cost myself.

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:27.567
Unfortunately, I'm getting this
great experience now.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
But have you found
that's happened before,

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
where people have said
to you like,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, I thought,
even just based on

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:34.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
the color palette
of the show --"

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.441 line:92%
-Well, first of all, yes.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to say that I think
it's very big of you

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:42.582
to share not just with me
but with all of America

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:45.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you feel that
your life is --

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's enriched.
-Enriched.

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-That's what I was gonna say.

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I will say
it's really lovely to hear,

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.392 line:92%
because I think there was --

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:54.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's always been
a slight --

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:58.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I do feel that the
show suffered a wee bit

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:01.034 size:84% position:42%
from a sort of an idea,
a preconceived idea,

00:05:01.034 --> 00:05:03.870
which often had nothing to do
with anyone having seen it.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:07.240
But because you could assume
there was those sort of things

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we knew and saw,
whether you saw,

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:11.711
the sort of titillating, you
know, and the candid language,

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.781
the salty dialogue,
and the costumes and the shoes.

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:18.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, in fact, I feel like the
show always offered up

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:22.555
actual profundity,
and the writing was really smart

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.723 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and moving and clever

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, I think,
beautifully illustrated

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
an attempt at finding love,
finding home, you know?

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I am so thrilled
to hear you --

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:34.267 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Also, I just didn't --

00:05:34.267 --> 00:05:36.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the part
that I'm really drawn to --

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.637 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And we're in Season 6.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're with Berger.
I hope it doesn't work out.

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:42.442 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, you know,
I thought the show

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:49.716
would have more of a bow on it,
if that makes sense.

00:05:49.716 --> 00:05:53.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
The characters
are so human and messy

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:54.787 line:92%
in a way that really resonates,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:57.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and especially,
like, where it starts.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.660
I mean, that's the part about it
that I did not realize,

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
because there
are certain shows you watch,

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, you can tune in
to a "Seinfeld" any season,

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there are
the same four characters.

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a very
different experience.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, the arc of it
is really an accomplishment.

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:15.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm now to the point --
'Cause when we started,

00:06:15.108 --> 00:06:17.944
my wife said it's, you know,
whatever, however many episodes,

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:18.878 line:92%
and I was like, "Oh, boy.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here we go."
-Yeah.

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:21.848
-"This seems like it's
going to be a lot of TV."

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now I'm like,
"We only have 17 left!"

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:28.621 size:84% position:42%
-Aww. That's so lovely.
-So thank you for that.

